{
  "description": "Evaluation-semantics vectors. These are the wire contract, not regression pins: any component that evaluates rules must produce these exact outcomes, or the same user would see different flag values depending on which component answered. Source: FortressFlag_Backend internal/clientapi/evaluate_vectors_test.go — the JSON is generated from that table, so every case here is one the backend evaluator actually ran against; published per ADR-0016. Flag configs use the server export's wire shape (server-contract-v1.md) so an SDK can feed them through its own payload decoder. Semantics in brief: rules walk in order, first match wins; conditions AND within a rule and an empty list holds vacuously; a condition whose tag key is absent does not hold; eq/neq are exact, case-sensitive, untrimmed string comparison; contains is a case-sensitive, untrimmed substring match (ADR-0023); semver operators split on dots, compare numerically, read missing components as 0, and an unparseable value on either side makes the condition not hold; an unknown operator never matches; a rolloutPercentage p matches only contexts whose bucket (vectors/buckets.json — the contextKey is the bucket input) is strictly below p, and a gated-out context falls THROUGH to later rules; no match serves the default, and a multivariate flag with no default has no value (noValue: the SDK serves its caller's fallback).",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "first-match-wins",
      "flag": { "kind": "boolean", "default": false, "rules": [
        { "conditions": [ { "tagKey": "cohort", "operator": "eq", "value": "beta" } ], "serve": true },
        { "conditions": [ { "tagKey": "cohort", "operator": "eq", "value": "beta" } ], "serve": false },
        { "conditions": [ { "tagKey": "appVersion", "operator": "semver_gte", "value": "2.0" } ], "serve": false }
      ] },
      "input": { "contextKey": "user-1", "flagKey": "dark-mode", "tags": { "cohort": "beta", "appVersion": "3.0" } },
      "expected": { "value": true }
    },
    {
